---
/**
 * WayfinderMap.astro — the picture on chapter 5's `wayfinder` Slide.
 * Comp E from wayfinder #98, rewritten out of prototype rules by #105.
 *
 * WHAT IT DRAWS: one map issue above a bracket, and the map's tickets below it
 * in four columns — Decided · Takeable now · Blocked · Not yet specified, with
 * Out of scope beneath the fog. The board is EMPTY MARKUP here; the Widget in
 * `wayfinder.widget.ts` fills it from `wayfinder-map.ts` on every Fragment
 * change, in both directions, so ← replays the walk backwards exactly.
 *
 * WHY THE STEP IS DRIVEN BY INVISIBLE FRAGMENTS. The comp first used a
 * presenter key, because reveal owns `n` and `p` and the obvious keys were
 * taken. Fragments cost NO key at all and make `→` and `←` behave the way they
 * do on every other Slide in the deck (#98). The three spans in the Fragment
 * row are counters, not content — the Widget reads how many are visible.
 *
 * ⚠ HISTORY COMPRESSES, and the build must keep it (#98). Nine full cards run
 * off the bottom of the canvas. A ticket closed on an EARLIER step drops to a
 * one-line ledger row; only the ones closing NOW show their answer. The Widget
 * owns that rule; this component only holds the slots it fills.
 *
 * THE RAIL IS NOT HERE. The Slide composes `PipelineRail` above this picture,
 * because the Rail belongs to the Slide and this component belongs to the map.
 */
import { MAP } from "../../lib/asml-ai/wayfinder-map";
---

{/* The parent: one issue, holding the destination and the live tally. It goes
    orange and lights its `/to-spec` chip on the last step, which is the beat
    the whole Slide is built to reach. */}
<div class="ch5-wf-map" data-wf-map>
  <span class="k">map</span>
  <p class="t">{MAP.title}</p>
  <p class="d">{MAP.destination}</p>
  <span class="tally" data-wf-tally></span>
  <span class="spec">/to-spec</span>
</div>

{/* The bracket: everything below hangs off the map above. Parent and child
    drawn structurally rather than stated in a caption (#98). */}
<div class="ch5-wf-tree"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

<div class="ch5-wf-board" data-wf-board>
  <div class="ch5-wf-col" data-wf-col="done">
    <h6>Decided</h6>
    <div data-wf-slot="done"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ch5-wf-col lit" data-wf-col="open">
    <h6>Takeable now</h6>
    <div data-wf-slot="open"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ch5-wf-col" data-wf-col="blocked">
    <h6>Blocked</h6>
    <div data-wf-slot="blocked"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ch5-wf-col" data-wf-col="fog">
    <h6>Not yet specified</h6>
    <div data-wf-slot="fog"></div>
    <p class="ch5-wf-outhead">Out of scope</p>
    <div data-wf-slot="out"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="ch5-wf-step" data-wf-step></p>

{/* Counters. Reveal advances on them; the Widget reads their count. They sit
    in a Fragment row, because that row is the element `fragSel` names (#113). */}
<div class="wf-frag-row" data-wf-frag-row aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="fragment" data-fragment-index="1"></span>
  <span class="fragment" data-fragment-index="2"></span>
  <span class="fragment" data-fragment-index="3"></span>
</div>
